{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.DimMasterPentagon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.DimMasterPentagon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dimMasterPentagon_refutable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dimMasterPentagon_refutable","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L262-L275","doc":"The class is **refutable**, which the previous `holds : Prop` carrier was not: the\none-point master datum satisfies the pentagon, so `master_holds` is discharged, but no\nspecialisation to `badPentagon` can exist — one would transport the pentagon onto a datum\nwhere it fails.\n\nStated as a theorem rather than left to the docstring because \"the carrier asserts something\"\nis precisely the property that was missing, and a reader should see it discharged rather than\ntake the prose's word. Note the refutation runs *through* `transport`, so it also exercises\nthe derivable half above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.badPentagon_not_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.badPentagon_not_holds","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L257-L260","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.badPentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.badPentagon","kind":"def","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L248-L255","doc":"A datum whose pentagon **fails**: one argument, operators `ℕ` under addition, and the\nconstant group-like `1`. The pentagon word reads `1 + 1 = (1 + 1) + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trivialPentagon_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trivialPentagon_holds","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L246-L246","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trivialPentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trivialPentagon","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L237-L244","doc":"The one-point datum: everything collapses, so the pentagon word is trivially satisfied.\nUsed only as the master half of the refutation below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon.specialises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon.specialises","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L235-L235","doc":"**The specialisation claim.** Each flavour is reached from the master by a\ncomposition-, product- and `Φ`-respecting surjection. By `PentagonSpecialisation.transport`\nthis forces every flavour's own pentagon, which is what \"unified algebraic ancestor\" has to\ndeliver. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon.master_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon.master_holds","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L230-L230","doc":"**The master identity.** The group-like assignment satisfies the pentagon word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon.mk","kind":"ctor","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L227-L227","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DimMasterPentagon","kind":"class","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L210-L235","doc":"**CONJECTURE (D17).** A master pentagon identity — Bourgine's, among group-like elements\nof the Ding–Iohara–Miki algebra `U_{q,t}(gl₁ double-hat)` — that specialises to each\noperational pentagon flavour.\n\n`master` and `flavour` are supplied **by the caller**, so the class is false at data that do\nnot satisfy these fields (see `dimMasterPentagon_refutable`). The flavour index `F` is\nlikewise the caller's: the tracker's five named flavours are not all presented in this word\nshape, and hard-coding them would assert more than the header supports.\n\n**This does not say the DIM algebra carries such a datum** — the corpus has no type for that\nalgebra, so the master datum is a parameter rather than a construction. That identification\nis the part of D17 that stays unformalised; see the header.\n\n**No instance is provided.** Downstream results consume this as\n`[DimMasterPentagon master flavour]` and are genuinely conditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:dim-master-pentagon ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:dim-master-pentagon","label":"conj:dim-master-pentagon","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.transport","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L199-L208","doc":"**The specialised datum satisfies the pentagon.** This is the derivable half of D17: if a\nmaster identity holds and a specialisation exists, the flavour identity is a consequence, not\na further assumption. Surjectivity of `onArgs` is exactly what extends `transport_apply` from\nthe image to all of the flavour's arguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.transport_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.transport_apply","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L186-L197","doc":"**The pentagon transports along a specialisation, on the image.** Surjectivity is not\nused here, which is the point: the flavour pentagon holds at every pair of arguments coming\nfrom the master, whether or not those exhaust the flavour's arguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.intertwines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.intertwines","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L184-L184","doc":"The two maps intertwine the group-like assignments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onArgs_compose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onArgs_compose","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L181-L181","doc":"The argument map preserves composition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onOps_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onOps_mul","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L179-L179","doc":"The operator map preserves the product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onArgs_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onArgs_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L177-L177","doc":"Every flavour argument is hit. Only this field is archimedean-free bookkeeping: it is\nwhat upgrades the pentagon on the image to the pentagon everywhere (see `transport`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onOps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onOps","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L174-L174","doc":"The map on operators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onArgs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.onArgs","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L172-L172","doc":"The map on arguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L170-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonSpecialisation","kind":"structure","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L165-L184","doc":"**A specialisation** of one pentagon datum to another: a map on arguments and a map on\noperators that together respect composition, the product, and the group-like assignment.\n\nThis is what \"the master pentagon *specialises to* a flavour\" has to mean if the flavour's\npentagon is to follow from the master's — and `transport` below shows that it does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Holds","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L156-L163","doc":"**The pentagon relation** for a datum: `Φ u ⬝ Φ v = (Φ v ⬝ Φ (u ⊛ v)) ⬝ Φ u`.\n\nThis is the Faddeev–Kashaev operator form `Φ(P) Φ(Q) = Φ(Q) Φ(P + Q) Φ(P)` with the\nparenthesisation written out. It is a predicate on data, not a conjecture carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Φ","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L154-L154","doc":"The group-like assignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.compose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.compose","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L152-L152","doc":"Composition of arguments (`P + Q` in Faddeev's form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.mul","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L150-L150","doc":"The operator product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Ops","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Ops","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L148-L148","doc":"Operators the assignment lands in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Args","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.Args","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L146-L146","doc":"Arguments of the group-like assignment (Faddeev's Weyl-pair operators `P`, `Q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L144-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PentagonDatum","kind":"structure","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/dim-master-pentagon.lean#L137-L154","doc":"**A pentagon datum.** An argument type with a composition `compose`, an operator type\nwith a product `mul`, and an assignment `Φ` of an operator to each argument — the data a\npentagon relation is stated about.\n\n`mul` is a bare binary operation, not a monoid multiplication: the pentagon word below is\nfully parenthesised, so associativity is never needed, and both the multiplicative operator\nform and the additive five-term form are instances. ","signatureChunk":0}]}